ernal system, calling setState in a callback function when external state changes.\n\nCalling setState synchronously within an effect body causes cascading renders that can hurt performance, and is not recommended. (https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect).\n\n/home/debjeet-dhar/Downloads/project/src/renderer/src/views/Notes.tsx:57:5\n  55 |\n  56 |   useEffect(() => {\n> 57 |     fetchNotes()\n     |     ^^^^^^^^^^ Avoid calling setState() directly within an effect\n  58 |     const interval = setInterval(fetchNotes, 3000) \n  59 |     return () => clearInterval(interval)\n  60 |   }, [])",["1794","1795"],"Error: Cannot access variable before it is declared\n\n`connectToDevice` is accessed before it is declared, which prevents the earlier access from updating when this value changes over time.\n\n/home/debjeet-dhar/Downloads/project/src/renderer/src/views/Phone.tsx:56:11\n  54 |           setIp(lastDevice.ip)\n  55 |           setPort(lastDevice.port)\n> 56 |           connectToDevice(lastDevice.ip, lastDevice.port)\n     |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `connectToDevice` accessed before it is declared\n  57 |         }\n  58 |       }\n  59 |     })\n\n/home/debjeet-dhar/Downloads/project/src/renderer/src/views/Phone.tsx:87:3\n   85 |   }\n   86 |\n>  87 |   const connectToDevice = async (targetIp: string, targetPort: string) => {\n      |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n>  88 |     if (!targetIp || !targetPort) return setErrorMsg('IP and Port are required.')\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n>  89 |     setStatus('connecting')\n      …\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 109 |     }\n      | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n> 110 |   }\n      | ^^^^ `connectToDevice` is declared here\n  111 |\n  112 |   const handleManualConnect = () => {\n  113 | 